// A `for` loop carrying a value that runs out (owner ruling 2026-09-29): no `break s` is taken,
// so the value is the `null` of its `string | null`. The proof prints that null's default, which
// a value read as non-null would trap on before printing.
//
// Format: scripts/capability-probes/matrix.py, whose docstring is the spec.
// @@PRELUDE@@
function words(): string[] { ["a", "bb", "ccc"] }
// @@VALUE@@
for s in words() { if s.length > 5 { break s } }
// @@TYPE@@
string | null
// @@PROOF@@
print(v ?? "none")
// @@WANT@@
none
// @@TEST@@
v == null
// @@HIT@@
print("none")
// @@MISS@@
print(v)
